From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] stresstest: Leave the timeout thread to the process exit

On Windows each test child starts a timeout thread and, once the file
has played, kills it with TerminateThread(). When the file is quick to
process, that can hit the thread while it is still starting up and
holds the loader lock. The child then deadlocks on the lock as it
exits, and the run hangs for good: i-110_062.amd did so here. Close
the handle and let ExitProcess() end the thread instead.

Upstream: not submitted; the code is from 24b3829c and is unchanged on
master
---
diff --git a/test/stresstest.cpp b/test/stresstest.cpp
--- a/test/stresstest.cpp
+++ b/test/stresstest.cpp
@@ -428,10 +428,10 @@
 	delete p;
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
-	if (hTimer) {
-		TerminateThread(hTimer, 0);
-		CloseHandle(hTimer);
-	}
+	// Leave the timer thread to the process exit: TerminateThread() can
+	// catch it still starting up with the loader lock held, and the exit
+	// then waits for that lock forever.
+	if (hTimer) CloseHandle(hTimer);
 #endif
 	return true;
 }
